  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms singleprofile (config_001, acc=0.485), confirming that aggregating multiple profiles is highly beneficial for the RNA modality. Image-only models are weak (0.208), so RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether transformer aggregation would further improve over avgpool for the multiprofile RNA setting. This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly one variable—aggregation method (transformer vs. avgpool)—while holding model_setting=rna_only, profile_setting=multiprofile, and rna_encoder=pca_n2000 fixed, matching the current best config_002. This is the highest-value next step because: (1) it directly extends the strongest finding, (2) it cleanly isolates the aggregation choice, (3) the result will inform which aggregation to pair with multimodal fusion in later experiments, and (4) with 6 experiments left, establishing the best RNA-only baseline before moving to multimodal is the most budget-efficient path."
}

